    "sourcePageUpdated": "2026-04-21",
    "definition": "Fatal accidents involving Part 121 air carriers, including accidents with fatalities on the ground. Flight exposure is departures compiled by the FAA.",
    "formula": "ratePerMillion = fatalAccidents / departures \u00d7 1,000,000",
    "complementFormula": "rateComplementPercent = 100 \u00d7 (1 - fatalAccidents / departures)",
    "safeShareIdentified": false,
    "limitations": [
      "This is a U.S.-operator passenger-and-cargo series, not global passenger flights.",
      "Fatal accidents include ground-handling fatalities; this is not a series of crashes or passenger deaths.",
      "The source reports accident events and departures, not a census of completed flights linked to accident outcomes. The rate complement is computable, but an exact observed safe-flight percentage is not identified. safePercent is deliberately null.",
      "The aircraft-detail audit finds one eligible aircraft in every fatal event in 2005\u20132024. There is no multiple-eligible-aircraft fatal collision adjustment in this period.",
      "The observation window ends in 2024. It excludes 2025 events and must not be represented as current 2026 risk.",
      "Zero observed fatal accidents is not proof of zero underlying risk.",
      "Annual rates fluctuate; the series does not show an uninterrupted decline.",
      "NTSB includes intentional acts in counts but excludes them from published rates. Table 12 lists none for scheduled Part 121 in this window, and direct count/departure rates reconcile with every annual published rate."
    ],
    "notes": [
      "flights is a compatibility alias for departures; use the label departures.",
      "No smoothing, interpolation, cross-source denominator join, or inferred passenger survival probability is used."
    ]
  },
